<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Sherley</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1581–<a href="/years/1628">1628</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Sherley was an English adventurer who, with his brother Anthony, travelled to the court of the Safavid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> at the end of the sixteenth century. He later served the shah as an envoy to European courts. The Sherley brothers assisted with Abbas I's military reforms, which created new corps of slave-soldier cavalry, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">musketeers</a> and artillerymen paid by the crown.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-sherley.jpg" alt="Robert Sherley" width="276" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anthony van Dyck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Van_Dyck_-_Sir_Robert_Shirley,_1622.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
